From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:52:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 135/342] meson_vdec: the warm-up decodes its picture for sure

The 16x16 picture is written twice: followed by nothing but zeros, the
firmware decoded it only sometimes (the next start code ends a slice), and
the first session after boot then had its first pictures wrong again
(1 boot of 2). With it twice and 100 ms for it: right in 5 boots of 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp  | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
index b67172af53..8ad01b1dc2 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
@@ -1114,9 +1114,14 @@ MesonVdec::_WarmUp(const meson_vdec_start& start, const void* userFirmware)
 	meson_vdec_start warmUp = start;
 	if (_StartSession(warmUp, userFirmware) != B_OK)
 		return;
-	memcpy(fInput.address, kH264EndOfStream, sizeof(kH264EndOfStream));
-	_Submit(sizeof(kH264EndOfStream), true);
-	// until the firmware got its frames and decoded the picture
+	// The picture twice: the second's start code ends the first's slice
+	// (followed by nothing but zeros, it was decoded only sometimes).
+	for (int32 i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+		memcpy(fInput.address, kH264EndOfStream, sizeof(kH264EndOfStream));
+		_Submit(sizeof(kH264EndOfStream), true);
+	}
+	// until the firmware got its frames and decoded the picture (which it
+	// doesn't report)
 	bigtime_t timeout = system_time() + 300000;
 	while (system_time() < timeout) {
 		InterruptsSpinLocker locker(fStateLock);
@@ -1126,7 +1131,7 @@ MesonVdec::_WarmUp(const meson_vdec_start& start, const void* userFirmware)
 			break;
 		snooze(2000);
 	}
-	snooze(20000);
+	snooze(100000);
 	INFO("warm-up session done\n");
 	_Stop(true);
 	fWarmedUp = true;
